if you've registered to vote by post  your postal vote will be delivered over  the coming weeks  inside you'll find your buck ballot  paper your postal voting statement two  envelopes clearly marked a and B and an  instruction sheet first separate your  postal voting statement from any  attached items next complete your ballot  paper in black ink on the reverse for  your ballot paper you will see your  ballot number place your completed  ballot paper into the envelope labeled  envelope a with your ballot paper number  clearly visible through the envelopes  window and seal the envelope next  complete your postal voting statement in  black ink this is the sheet that has the  date of the election and your ward at  the top your postal voting statement has  a return address addressed to the  returning officer on the back place your  voting statement together with envelope  a into envelope B with the return  address visible through the window of  the envelope seal envelope B now you're  all done you don't need a stamp and can  post the envelope at any post office or  postal box voting by post is easy the  deadline to apply for a postal vote is  Monday the 15th of April you can find  the postal vote application form online  on the gov you K website
 

